  "body": "### Features\n- feat(release): plan shows who gets each release; dry_run input (D-REL-WHO-1)\n\n### Fixes\n- fix(kiro): Kiro CLI 3.0 tool ids, stdin prompt, recall stdout and KIRO_HOME rule\n- fix(setup): OpenCode 2 list check reads the config the CLI loads; a broken Copilot CLI is SKIPPED with its own fix line (#1308)\n- fix(opencode): doctor finds the plugin's own bundle dir and accepts the OpenCode 2.x plugins list (#1306, #1307)\n- fix(setup): trust Codex 0.166 plugin hooks with trusted_hash + trusted_content_hash so an upgrade keeps them trusted (D-NI-CODEX-TRUST-4)\n- fix(intake): score issue reports, keep one comment, leave issue state to maintainers\n\n### Who gets this\n\nOne version on both channels: the release commit on main (GitHub) and npm.\n\n| Agent | Channel | Update with |\n|---|---|---|\n| Claude Code | GitHub | `claude plugin update context-mode@context-mode` |\n| Codex | GitHub, npm for the one-time hook trust step | `codex plugin marketplace upgrade context-mode` |\n| Gemini CLI | GitHub | `gemini extensions update context-mode` |\n| Qwen Code | GitHub | `qwen extensions update context-mode` |\n| Copilot CLI | npm | `context-mode upgrade` |\n| VS Code (Copilot) | npm | `context-mode upgrade` |\n| Kiro | npm | `context-mode upgrade` |\n| ZCode | npm | `context-mode upgrade` |\n| Pi | npm | `pi update --extensions` |\n| OpenCode | npm | `opencode plugin update` |"
